# Workflow drill notes

## Contradicted Decisions

None identified in the supplied workflow decisions and retained evals.

## Gaps

- FLOW-001, target module `workflow`: Claim creation uses an atomic ref update, but preparing the projected change document and snapshot happens immediately before that update; a simultaneous claimant may briefly see its own unclaimed document edit before a failed claim is rolled back.
- FLOW-073, target module `workflow`: Attempt restoration restores whole saved files touched by the attempt. It does not merge concurrent edits to the same file made after the attempt was saved.
- FLOW-117, target module `workflow`: PR body file categories are represented by paths. Detailed per-phase category labels and metadata are not fully rendered.
- no spec, target module `workflow`: The supplied workspace has no `go.mod`; `SYSTEM.md` prohibits local builds and tests, so compilation and behavior remain for the outside verifier.

